  "live_records": {
    "q-143461": {
      "dom_id": "step-q143461",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following joint probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}24xy, & \\,0<x<1,0<y<1-x \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFind $P(Y<X\\,|\\,X=\\frac{1}{3}).$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that \n\n$$\nP(Y\\in A\\,|\\,X=x)={\\int }_{A}{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y,\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ is the conditional probability density function of $Y$ given $X=x.$ \n\nUsing the formula for the marginal density function for $X,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1-x}24xy\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =24x{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =24x{[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{1-x} \\\\  & =12x(1-x)^{2}-0 \\\\  & =12x(x-1)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the full expression for ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)={\\begin{aligned}12x(x-1)^{2}, & \\,0<x<1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow recall that the conditional probability density function of $Y$ given $X=x$ for two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)}.\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability density function for $X$ and $Y,$ and\n\n- ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the marginal density function for $X.$\n\nNow, for $0<x<1,0<y<1-x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{24xy}{12x(x-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2y}{(x-1)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor other values of $x$ and $y,$ the function $f(x,y)$ equals $0.$ As a result, ${f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ will be equal to $0$ too.\n\nTherefore, the conditional probability density function is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2y}{(x-1)^{2}}, & \\,0<x<1,0<y<1-x \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute our probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y<X\\,|\\,X=\\frac{1}{3}) & =P(Y<\\frac{1}{3}\\,|\\,X=\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/3}{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x=\\frac{1}{3})\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/3}\\frac{2y}{{(\\frac{1}{3}-1)}^{2}}\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1/3}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{1/3} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}(\\frac{1}{18}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
