    "q-143574": {
      "dom_id": "step-q143574",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following joint probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}8xy, & \\,0\\le x\\le y,\\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFind $P(\\frac{1}{4}<X<\\frac{1}{2}\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{2}{3}).$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that \n\n$$\nP(Y\\in A\\,|\\,X=x)={\\int }_{A}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ is the conditional probability density function of $X$ given $Y=y.$ \n\nUsing the formula for the marginal density function for $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{y}8xy\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8y{\\int }_{0}^{y}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8y{[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{y} \\\\  & =4y({y}^{2}-0) \\\\  & =4{y}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the full expression for ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)={\\begin{aligned}4{y}^{3}, & \\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow recall that the conditional probability density function of $X$ given $Y=y$ for two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)}.\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability density function for $X$ and $Y,$ and\n\n- ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the marginal density function for $Y.$\n\nNow, for $0\\le x\\le 1,0\\le y\\le x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)} \\\\  & =\\frac{8xy}{4{y}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{{y}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor other values of $x$ and $y,$ the function $f(x,y)$ equals $0.$ As a result, ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ will be equal to $0$ too.\n\nTherefore, the conditional probability density function is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x}{{y}^{2}}, & \\,0\\le x\\le y,\\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute our probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\frac{1}{4}<X<\\frac{1}{2}\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{2}{3}) & ={\\int }_{1/4}^{1/2}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y=\\frac{2}{3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/4}^{1/2}\\frac{2x}{{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}{\\int }_{1/4}^{1/2}2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}{[{x}^{2}]}_{1/4}^{1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}(\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{16}) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}(\\frac{3}{16}) \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{64}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
