    "q-143634": {
      "dom_id": "step-q143634",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following joint probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2y(2x+3y)}{5}, & \\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression of the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ for $1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the formula for the marginal density function for $Y,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{2y(2x+3y)}{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(\\frac{4xy}{5}+\\frac{6{y}^{2}}{5})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{2{x}^{2}y}{5}+\\frac{6x{y}^{2}}{5}]}_{x=1}^{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{8y}{5}+\\frac{12{y}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{2y}{5}-\\frac{6{y}^{2}}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{6{y}^{2}}{5}+\\frac{6y}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{6y(y+1)}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the full expression for ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6y(y+1)}{5}, & \\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow recall that the conditional probability density function of $X$ given $Y=y$ for two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability density function for $X$ and $Y,$ and\n\n- ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the marginal density function for $Y.$\n\nNow, for $1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{2y(2x+3y)}{5})}{(\\frac{6y(y+1)}{5})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x+3y}{3(y+1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor other values of $x$ and $y,$ the function $f(x,y)$ equals $0.$ As a result, ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ will be equal to $0$ too.\n\nTherefore, the conditional probability density function is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+3y}{3(y+1)}, & \\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
